     <a class="skip-link" href="#maincontent">Skip to main content</a>
     <div class="page-shell">
       <header class="topbar">
         <div class="brand">
           <div class="brand-badge" aria-hidden="true">C</div>
           <span>Cat Care FAQ</span>
         </div>
       </header>

       <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
         <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
           <p class="eyebrow">Trusted cat basics</p>
           <h1 id="hero-title">Everything cat parents ask first.</h1>
           <p>
             Browse quick answers about behavior, feeding, sleep, and everyday care. Each topic
             expands in place so you can scan fast and dive deeper only when you need to.
           </p>
           <div class="stats" aria-label="FAQ highlights">
             <div class="stat-card">
               <strong>6 FAQs</strong>
               <span>Most common cat questions</span>
             </div>
             <div class="stat-card">
               <strong>Beginner-friendly</strong>
               <span>Short, practical guidance</span>
             </div>
             <div class="stat-card">
               <strong>Fast to scan</strong>
               <span>Collapsed by default</span>
             </div>
           </div>
         </section>

         <section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
           <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
           <div class="faq-grid">
             <div class="example">
               <h3 class="question">
                 <button
                   class="trigger"
                   type="button"
                   aria-expanded="true"
                   aria-controls="faq-answer-1"
                 >
                   Why do cats purr?
                   <span class="trigger-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                 </button>
               </h3>
               <div class="details" id="faq-answer-1">
                 <p>
                   Cats often purr when they feel safe and content, but they may also purr to soothe
                   themselves when stressed or recovering. Context matters, so notice their body
                   language, appetite, and energy too.
                 </p>
               </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
               <h3 class="question">
                 <button
                   class="trigger"
                   type="button"
                   aria-expanded="true"
                   aria-controls="faq-answer-2"
                 >
                   How often should I feed my cat?
                   <span class="trigger-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                 </button>
               </h3>
               <div class="details" id="faq-answer-2">
                 <p>
                   Most adult cats do well with measured meals twice a day, while kittens usually need
                   more frequent feeding. Use portion guidance from your food brand and your vet, and
                   always keep fresh water available.
                 </p>
               </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
               <h3 class="question">
                 <button
                   class="trigger"
                   type="button"
                   aria-expanded="true"
                   aria-controls="faq-answer-3"
                 >
                   Why does my cat knead blankets or pillows?
                   <span class="trigger-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                 </button>
               </h3>
               <div class="details" id="faq-answer-3">
                 <p>
                   Kneading is a common comfort behavior that starts in kittenhood. Many cats keep it
                   because it feels relaxing and familiar, especially when they are sleepy, cozy, or
                   near a trusted person.
                 </p>
               </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
               <h3 class="question">
                 <button
                   class="trigger"
                   type="button"
                   aria-expanded="true"
                   aria-controls="faq-answer-4"
                 >
                   How much sleep is normal for a cat?
                   <span class="trigger-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                 </button>
               </h3>
               <div class="details" id="faq-answer-4">
                 <p>
                   Many cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day, and some rest even longer. It is
                   usually normal, but a sudden change in sleep patterns paired with low appetite or
                   unusual behavior is worth discussing with a veterinarian.
                 </p>
               </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
               <h3 class="question">
                 <button
                   class="trigger"
                   type="button"
                   aria-expanded="true"
                   aria-controls="faq-answer-5"
                 >
                   What kind of toys do indoor cats need?
                   <span class="trigger-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                 </button>
               </h3>
               <div class="details" id="faq-answer-5">
                 <p>
                   Indoor cats benefit from toys that let them stalk, chase, climb, and puzzle-solve.
                   Rotate toys every few days to keep them interesting, and mix active play with calm
                   enrichment like window perches or scratchers.
                 </p>
               </div>
             </div>

             <div class="example">
               <h3 class="question">
                 <button
                   class="trigger"
                   type="button"
                   aria-expanded="true"
                   aria-controls="faq-answer-6"
                 >
                   How can I help a shy cat feel safer at home?
                   <span class="trigger-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                 </button>
               </h3>
               <div class="details" id="faq-answer-6">
                 <p>
                   Give a shy cat quiet hiding spots, predictable routines, and the choice to come to
                   you on their own timeline. A calm space, vertical perches, and short daily play
                   sessions can help build confidence without forcing interaction.
                 </p>
               </div>
             </div>
           </div>
           <p class="footer-note">
             These answers are for general education and are not a substitute for veterinary advice.
           </p>
         </section>
       </main>
     </div>

     <script>
       const faqButtons = document.querySelectorAll(".trigger");

       faqButtons.forEach((button) => {
         const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));

         if (!details) {
           return;
         }

         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
         details.hidden = true;

         button.addEventListener("click", () => {
           const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
           button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
           details.hidden = isExpanded;
         });

         button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
           if (event.key === "Escape" && button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
             button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
             details.hidden = true;
             button.focus();
           }
         });
       });
     </script>
   </body>
 </html>

